        "problem": "Evaluate $\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u20614).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u20614)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u20614) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4-{4}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{15}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
